    narr:narration """This position holds that markdown timing and shelf labeling move together: [day-old loaves drop to half price at two in the afternoon rather than at close, because nobody is left to buy them at close](narr:Expr_20261015_3_Batch2Bakery20261015222221_h0dbadf4ef6be_1), and [the shelf card changes at two as well so the price is never a surprise at the till](narr:Expr_20261015_3_Batch2Bakery20261015222221_h0dbadf4ef6be_2). Both members voice it as a claim argued by reason, framed as market pricing.""" ;
